course: dictionary
lesson: 4302
title: Grinders: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so context decides which one you need. Look at the words around it. Is the sentence about food, metal, or teeth? Those clues tell you the meaning.
explain: Kitchen words give one clue: «a coffee grinder» and «a pepper grinder» are machines that crush things into small bits or powder. In a workshop, an «angle grinder» has a spinning disc that smooths or cuts metal or stone. Same word, different job.
explain: Now look at this sentence: «A house mouse has 16 teeth: 4 front gnawing teeth and 12 back grinders, with a big gap between them and no canines.» Gnawing and teeth are the clues, so here a grinder is a back tooth. Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: A grinder is a machine or tool that crushes something into small bits or powder.
fact: A pepper grinder crushes peppercorns into powder for your food.
fact: An angle grinder is a power tool with a spinning disc that smooths or cuts metal or stone.
fact: Informally, a grinder is a back tooth, also called a molar.
fact: In the US, a grinder is a long sandwich, also called a sub.
exercise: «A pepper grinder» in a kitchen does what? | Keeps the kitchen cool | *Crushes peppercorns into small bits | Makes the bread rise | Cuts through steel pipes
exercise: What does the spinning disc of an angle grinder do? | Makes music | *Smooths or cuts metal or stone | Stores heat for cooking | Holds the tooth in place
exercise: In «12 back grinders», what is a grinder? | A front tooth for gnawing | A gap between teeth | *A back tooth | A kind of cat's claw
test: The mouse sentence says «4 front gnawing teeth and 12 back grinders». How many back grinders does the mouse have? | *12 | 16 | 4 | 8
test: Which machine would you use to turn whole peppercorns into powder for dinner? | A meat grinder that makes sausages | A workshop saw | *A pepper grinder | An angle grinder
exam: Read: «The workshop had a loud angle grinder cutting through steel.» What does grinder mean here? | A machine that crushes food | A long sandwich | *A power tool with a spinning disc that cuts metal | A back tooth
